Blocked-by: #2318
Not-before: 2026-10-02T09:00:00Z
Model: opus
Automerge: anything

<!-- filed by /do-later -->

Remove the engine's legacy tolerance for a check's retired `severity: "blocking" | "advisory"` spelling, one week after #2318 renamed it to `on_fail: "block" | "advise"` (owner decision, 2026-09-25: a one-week window, auto-merge when green).

## First, read the premise

Check that `main` carries #2318: `engine/checks/helpers/findings.mjs` exports `LEGACY_ON_FAIL`, and `engine/migrations/2026-09-25-on-fail-rename/migration.mjs` exists. If either is missing, #2318 never merged. Converge as `action` naming it, and change nothing.

## What the tolerance is

Both carry `// @legacy-tolerance … retire:#2319`:

- `LEGACY_ON_FAIL` in `engine/checks/helpers/findings.mjs`: the engine still reads `severity` on a rule, a declared check, a finding and a settings override value. Its advisory is `legacy-shape-in-use`, which names each old spelling a member still holds.
- `LEGACY_SEVERITY_MIRROR` (same file, `advisory:none`): every finding also carries `severity` mirroring its `on_fail`. The holder is a member's own local-pack **tests** that read `finding.severity`. No advisory can reach a test's assertion, so after this change such a test fails on the member's next engine update and the member fixes it in its own repo. That is the accepted break.

What moved members off it: the engine record `on-fail-rename` (codemod `renameOnFail`) respells the member's settings overrides, local declared checks and local check modules on its update to engine 60925.1. It stays as history; a lagging member still gets it on its first update.

## The change

Apply the patch below, which was written and tested against #2318's head. Drift since then may need a hand rebase: keep the intent, which is to delete every read of the old spelling.

Then append provenance entries dated the day you run:
- `claudinite-lifecycle legacy-shape-in-use`: `scope-changed` (no longer reports the retired `severity` spelling; the engine stopped reading it; Mechanism: this check).
- `claudinite consumer-safe-change`: `reworded` (reads `on_fail` only).

Run the whole suite (`node --test $(git ls-files '*.test.mjs')`), `node engine/checks/check_the_world.mjs` and `node engine/checks/check_the_work.mjs`. `git grep -n "retire:#2319"` must print nothing.

Do not put `Closes #2319` in the PR body: the queue closes this item.

